Strategy: // CSD_RATIONALE_BEGIN
// The best prior strategy already had the strongest accuracy, so this revision
// keeps its overall shape and makes two targeted changes aimed directly at the
// observed failures.
//
// 1) Guarantee at least one `<< ... >>` span instead of waiting for the model to
// emit `"<<"` on its own. The evaluation showed many outputs still had no
// delimiters at all. To fix that, the strategy force-opens a constrained span
// once after a short amount of unconstrained prefix generation (or immediately
// if we started inside one). This preserves the natural lead-in text while
// making delimiter presence reliable.
//
// 2) Reduce unterminated spans by reserving room to close. Once inside a
// constrained span, if only one decoding step remains and the current prefix is
// complete, we spend that final step on `CloseConstrainedSpan`; otherwise, if
// only one step remains and the prefix is not complete, we stop rather than
// append another token that cannot be closed. This directly targets the
// previously common `<<` without matching `>>` failures.
//
// Inside arithmetic spans, the strategy still uses parser-checked generation.
// It prefers a penalized constrained step right after rollback recovery, and
// otherwise uses adaptive group-boosted constrained sampling. The rollback logic
// from the best prior attempt is retained because it improved correctness on
// malformed local continuations: after a narrow dead-end, we roll back to a
// boundary token and penalize the excluded divergence token on the next step.
// Overall, this is the prior high-accuracy design plus explicit one-time span
// insertion and stronger end-of-budget closure discipline.
// CSD_RATIONALE_END
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_BEGIN
// parser_validity:
//   - Forced-open / unconstrained branch: when we open a span with
//     OpenConstrainedSpan, currentConstrainedOut becomes [], and
//     parser.IsValidPrefix([]) is a precondition; if we stay outside, the
//     implication is vacuous.
//   - Close branch: CloseConstrainedSpan sets insideConstrainedOut := false, so
//     the implication becomes vacuous.
//   - Penalized/adaptive constrained append branch: the sampling helper returns
//     either eosToken or a token that keeps the constrained prefix parser-valid;
//     on non-EOS, AppendConstrainedToken preserves validity.
//   - Rollback recovery sub-branch: RollbackAndExclude guarantees the repaired
//     constrained prefix is parser-valid, and we assign that repaired prefix to
//     currentConstrainedOut.
//
// suffix:
//   - Forced-open / unconstrained branch: after OpenConstrainedSpan,
//     currentConstrainedOut == [], which matches the empty suffix of generated;
//     otherwise we remain outside constrained mode, so the implication is
//     vacuous.
//   - Close branch: after CloseConstrainedSpan we are outside constrained mode,
//     so the suffix invariant is vacuous.
//   - Constrained append branch: AppendConstrainedToken appends the same token
//     to generated and currentConstrainedOut, preserving suffix equality.
//   - Rollback recovery sub-branch: RollbackAndExclude returns a repaired prefix
//     of the old constrained content; trimming exactly the dropped suffix from
//     generated restores generated[|generated|-|repaired|..] == repaired.
//
// cost accounting:
//   - We return cost := steps. Every non-breaking branch increments steps by 1
//     after exactly one cost-bumping helper call: UnconstrainedStep,
//     OpenConstrainedSpan, CloseConstrainedSpan, PenalizedConstrainedStep, or
//     AdaptiveConstrainedStep.
//   - The rollback/query work is nested under a branch that already consumed its
//     one step, so it needs no extra bump. Break branches happen immediately
//     after a step or before taking any further action, so cost := steps stays
//     within maxSteps.
//
// progress bound:
//   - Unconstrained append branch: exactly one token is appended and steps is
//     incremented by 1.
//   - Forced-open branch: OpenConstrainedSpan appends exactly one delimiter
//     token and steps is incremented by 1.
//   - Close branch: CloseConstrainedSpan appends at most one token and steps is
//     incremented by 1.
//   - Constrained append branch: after one constrained sampling step,
//     AppendConstrainedToken appends exactly one token; rollback may then shrink
//     generated, which only makes |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + steps
//     easier to satisfy. Immediate-break branches append no further tokens.
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_END
