Strategy: // CSD_RATIONALE_BEGIN
// The prior strategy failed mainly because it waited for the model to *voluntarily*
// emit "<<" during unconstrained decoding; traces showed that almost never happened,
// so many answers had no << >> spans at all. The revised strategy therefore makes
// delimiter insertion explicit: after a short unconstrained lead-in, if we are still
// outside a span and have budget left, we directly open one with OpenConstrainedSpan.
// Inside the span we generate only parser-valid arithmetic content, and as soon as
// the arithmetic prefix is complete we immediately close it with CloseConstrainedSpan.
// This directly targets the missing-delimiter and unterminated-span failures.
//
// A second change is to use chunked unconstrained decoding before the forced opening.
// That reduces runtime versus token-by-token free decoding while still letting the
// model produce a short natural-language setup such as "We compute". After the first
// constrained computation is closed, we allow a small amount of unconstrained trailing
// text, but we do not rely on further spontaneous openings. This biases outputs toward
// containing at least one well-formed <<arithmetic>> computation, which is the task's
// key requirement, while keeping the overall strategy simple and provable.
// CSD_RATIONALE_END
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_BEGIN
// parser_validity: In the unconstrained-chunk branch we remain outside, so the
//   implication is vacuous; if the chunk stops on an open span, the helper enters
//   constrained mode with currentConstrainedOut == [], and parser.IsValidPrefix([])
//   holds by precondition. In the forced-open branch, OpenConstrainedSpan likewise
//   sets currentConstrainedOut := [] and insideConstrainedOut := true, preserving
//   validity. In the close branch, CloseConstrainedSpan sets insideConstrainedOut
//   to false, making the implication vacuous. In the constrained-step branch,
//   AdaptiveConstrainedStep returns either eosToken or a parser-valid next token;
//   on the non-EOS path, AppendConstrainedToken preserves parser validity.
// suffix: While outside constrained mode, the suffix invariant is vacuous. When a
//   chunk stops on an open span or when we force-open, currentConstrainedOut becomes
//   empty, so generated[|generated|-0..] == [] holds trivially. In the close branch
//   we leave constrained mode, so the implication is vacuous afterward. In the
//   constrained append branch, AppendConstrainedToken appends the same next token to
//   both generated and currentConstrainedOut, preserving exact suffix equality.
// cost accounting: We use a local steps counter and return cost := steps. Every
//   non-breaking branch strictly increases steps by the amount of generation done:
//   UnconstrainedChunk adds stepsUsed, OpenConstrainedSpan adds 1, CloseConstrainedSpan
//   adds 1, and AdaptiveConstrainedStep + AppendConstrainedToken adds 1. Breaks occur
//   immediately after a helper that already consumed its counted cost, so cost := steps
//   at the end satisfies cost <= maxSteps.
// progress bound: UnconstrainedChunk appends exactly stepsUsed tokens and we add the
//   same amount to steps, so |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + steps is preserved.
//   OpenConstrainedSpan appends one delimiter token and we increment steps by 1;
//   CloseConstrainedSpan appends at most one token and also increments steps by 1.
//   The constrained-step branch either breaks on EOS with no append, or appends one
//   token through AppendConstrainedToken and increments steps by 1. Thus every
//   non-breaking branch preserves the linear bound and strictly decreases
//   maxSteps - steps.
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_END
generated := generatedPrefix;
insideConstrainedOut := insideConstrained;
currentConstrainedOut := currentConstrained;
cost := 0;

var steps: nat := 0;
var openedAnySpan: bool := insideConstrained;
var trailingMode: bool := false;

while steps < maxSteps
  invariant 0 <= steps <= maxSteps
  invariant lm.ValidTokensIdsLogits()
  invariant !insideConstrainedOut ==> currentConstrainedOut == []
  invariant insideConstrainedOut ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentConstrainedOut)
  invariant insideConstrainedOut ==> |currentConstrainedOut| <= |generated|
  invariant insideConstrainedOut ==> generated[|generated| - |currentConstrainedOut|..] == currentConstrainedOut
  invariant |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + steps
  invariant cost == 0
  decreases maxSteps - steps
{
  if insideConstrainedOut {
    var complete := parser.IsCompletePrefix(currentConstrainedOut);
    if complete {
      var closedGenerated, closedInside, closedCurrent := helpers.CloseConstrainedSpan(
        lm, parser, generated, currentConstrainedOut
      );
      generated := closedGenerated;
      insideConstrainedOut := closedInside;
      currentConstrainedOut := closedCurrent;
      trailingMode := true;
      steps := steps + 1;
    } else {
      var stablePrefix := generated[..|generated| - |currentConstrainedOut|];
      var next := helpers.AdaptiveConstrainedStep(
